# PER-PAGE METADATA (App Router `metadata` export)

For each page, use Next.js App Router's `metadata` export (or `generateMetadata`) with these values. Because `output: 'export'` runs at build time, these will appear in the static HTML `<head>` automatically.

Each page must produce:
- `<title>` — exact title per page above
- `<meta name="description">` — exact description per page above
- `<link rel="canonical" href="...">` — exact canonical per page above
- `<meta property="og:title">`, `<meta property="og:description">`, `<meta property="og:url">`, `<meta property="og:type" content="website">`, `<meta property="og:site_name" content="NeedAWebsite">`
- `<meta property="og:image" content="https://needawebsite.in/og-image.png">` — Phase 1 references this tag; the file is supplied in Phase 2, so leave the tag in place.
- `<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">`, `<meta name="twitter:title">`, `<meta name="twitter:description">`, `<meta name="twitter:image">`

Use `metadataBase: new URL('https://needawebsite.in')` in the root layout's metadata for canonical resolution.

